WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.669 --> 00:00:05.440
With a bullet to the face and a bunch of traumatic
memories rising to the surface, the first

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:07.680
trailer for Sony's Bloodshot is finally here.

00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:11.600
And after what's felt like an eternity of
waiting, the footage surely should have been

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:15.820
met with thunderous applause and about a thousand
posts per minute on social media.

00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:20.500
Vin Diesel playing Ray Garrison, a murdered
Marine who comes back to life and is infused

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:23.920
with nanotechnology to become the killing
machine known as Bloodshot?

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:28.620
Academy Award-winning screenwriter Eric Heisserer
joining forces with scribe Jeff Wadlow to

00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:29.600
pen the script?

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:33.879
First-time feature film director Dave Wilson
bringing the famous Valiant Comics character

00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:36.220
to the big screen for the first time ever?

00:00:36.460 --> 00:00:40.000
Sounds like a recipe for comic book movie
success that would start with the release

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:41.160
of the first trailer.

00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:46.539
But when Sony dropped the first Bloodshot
trailer on Monday, October 21, many fans were

00:00:46.540 --> 00:00:48.280
left disappointed by what they saw.

00:00:48.449 --> 00:00:52.079
The biggest gripe some fans have about the
first Bloodshot trailer is that it doesn't

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:57.280
feel like a trailer at all it feels like an
entire film condensed into 2 minutes and 40

00:00:57.280 --> 00:00:57.780
seconds.

00:00:57.980 --> 00:01:02.200
Many people across Twitter and in the comments
section of the trailer on YouTube expressed

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:06.760
dissatisfaction over the trailer seemingly
spoiling all the narrative beats of the film.

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:08.040
One user tweeted:

00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:10.460
"Whoever made this trailer, should be fired.

00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:12.880
Spoiled the entire movie in just 2 [minutes]."

00:01:13.340 --> 00:01:17.390
Another wondered why the trailer didn't show
off just "a few action sequences" instead

00:01:17.390 --> 00:01:19.980
of apparently laying all its cards out on
the table.

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:20.820
They wrote:

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:23.280
"Seriously why do they give away the whole
plot?

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:26.640
Only a few action sequences should be enough
to build some hype."

00:01:26.940 --> 00:01:31.340
Over on YouTube, even more people were upset
over the evidently spoiler-heavy trailer.

00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:35.960
One user wrote, quote, "When the movie comes
out I'd say I watched [it] already just from

00:01:35.960 --> 00:01:36.720
this trailer."

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:40.200
Another reason some fans were let down by
the brand-new Bloodshot trailer?

00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:44.600
They feel Bloodshot doesn't look like Bloodshot
he just looks like Vin Diesel.

00:01:44.740 --> 00:01:47.140
One less-than-impressed Twitter user wrote:

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:51.000
"Looks very generic, I would have preferred
something that embraced its comic origins

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:51.500
more.

00:01:51.640 --> 00:01:54.760
I mean, he doesn't look like Bloodshot at
all, it's just Vin Diesel.

00:01:54.860 --> 00:01:59.439
In not embracing the look of the comic they've
made it seem way more bland and generic."

00:01:59.439 --> 00:02:03.630
Someone else tweeted, quote, "I don't know
a ton about Bloodshot, but I'm fairly sure

00:02:03.630 --> 00:02:05.880
he doesn't just look like regular Vin Diesel."

00:02:06.060 --> 00:02:10.340
One fan on Reddit was particularly displeased
with the character design — or, perhaps

00:02:10.340 --> 00:02:14.060
more accurately, lack thereof — shown in
the first Bloodshot trailer.

00:02:14.240 --> 00:02:16.440
In a thread on the movies subreddit, they
wrote:

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:20.879
"I'm usually not a stickler for this sort
of thing, but the most core aspect of the

00:02:20.879 --> 00:02:25.420
character design is that his body is pure
white, he has a giant red dot on his chest,

00:02:25.420 --> 00:02:29.549
and his eyes are red, and that was completely
abandoned for peachy Vin [Diesel].

00:02:29.549 --> 00:02:32.989
I guess it just feels like they didn't even
really wanna try to make this an adaptation

00:02:32.989 --> 00:02:33.620
of the comic.

00:02:33.800 --> 00:02:36.120
Maybe I'm bitter, I just wanted more from
this."

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:40.300
Of course, there's a strong chance that the
reason why Bloodshot simply looks like everyday

00:02:40.319 --> 00:02:44.690
Vin Diesel in this first trailer is because
his transformation into the character fans

00:02:44.690 --> 00:02:48.860
know and love from the Valiant Comics will
happen elsewhere in the film, during a sequence

00:02:48.860 --> 00:02:49.980
not shown in the trailer.

00:02:50.330 --> 00:02:54.100
Since the footage did reveal quite a bit about
the plot of Bloodshot, perhaps the film's

00:02:54.110 --> 00:02:57.900
team is holding off on revealing Bloodshot
in all his glory until later.

00:02:57.900 --> 00:03:01.879
Plus, it's worth noting that the trailer does
feature a blink-and-you'll-miss-it shot of

00:03:01.880 --> 00:03:04.930
a pale-skinned, red-eyed Diesel so who knows?

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:09.940
Thankfully for Sony executives, the Bloodshot
cast and creative team, and fans at home,

00:03:09.940 --> 00:03:12.340
this is just the first taste of the forthcoming
flick.

00:03:12.540 --> 00:03:18.420
As Bloodshot nears its February 21, 2020 release
date, there will likely be several more trailers,

00:03:18.430 --> 00:03:22.750
teasers, TV spots, and promotional material
rolled out to boost anticipation.

00:03:22.750 --> 00:03:26.350
If you weren't blown away by this initial
trailer, perhaps a future one will change

00:03:26.350 --> 00:03:26.920
your mind.

